@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# Stage 6 Cutover — Permanent Redirects + Print Base URL
+
+**Status: DOCUMENTED ONLY — nothing here has been executed.** These are the
+two server-side switches that make the Stage 5 write-ownership lock-down
+permanent, plus one low-priority cleanup. Do these together in one window;
+both are trivially reversible.
+
+## 1. Permanent server-side 301s (webapp → alts)
+
+Stage 5 shipped *client-side* redirects (`AltsRedirect`, `AltsGarmentRedirect`)
+so the SPA bounces ticket routes to alts. Cutover makes them server-side and
+permanent in the root `vercel.json` (the app.lstailors.com deployment):
+
+1. Flip the four existing QR redirects (`/g/…`, `/garments/…`, `/t/…`,
+   `/e-ticket/…`) from `"permanent": false` → `"permanent": true`.
+2. Add the lock-down routes:
+
+```json
+{ "source": "/intake/alterations",            "destination": "https://alts.lstailors.com/intake/alterations",            "permanent": true },
+{ "source": "/orders/alterations",            "destination": "https://alts.lstailors.com/orders/alterations",            "permanent": true },
+{ "source": "/orders/alterations/:ticketName","destination": "https://alts.lstailors.com/orders/alterations/:ticketName","permanent": true },
+{ "source": "/orders/alterations/:ticketName/tags",    "destination": "https://alts.lstailors.com/orders/alterations/:ticketName/tags",    "permanent": true },
+{ "source": "/orders/alterations/:ticketName/receipt", "destination": "https://alts.lstailors.com/orders/alterations/:ticketName/receipt", "permanent": true },
+{ "source": "/admin/board",                   "destination": "https://alts.lstailors.com/board",                          "permanent": true }
+```
+
+Notes:
+- 301s are cached aggressively by browsers — only flip `permanent: true`
+  once alts routes are confirmed stable in production.
+- The client-side `AltsRedirect` pages stay in the webapp as a fallback for
+  any deployment path that bypasses Vercel redirects; they can be deleted a
+  release after the 301s ship.
+- Do NOT redirect `/orders/custom` or `/intake/custom` — custom orders remain
+  admin-owned.
+
+## 2. ERPNext `LSH Print Settings.app_base_url` → alts
+
+Printed QR codes (hang tags, tickets, labels) embed URLs built from
+`LSH Print Settings.app_base_url`, which still points at app.lstailors.com.
+After cutover every freshly printed QR should land directly on alts instead
+of bouncing through a redirect.
+
+A ready-made script already exists — run it against production ERP when
+cutting over (requires ERP admin API creds in env):
+
+```
+bun backend/src/scripts/set-alts-print-base-url.ts
+```
+
+It flips `LSH Print Settings.app_base_url` → `https://alts.lstailors.com`
+and prints the before/after values. Old printed tags keep working via the
+301s from §1.
+
+## 3. Low-priority cleanup — auth localStorage dual-write
+
+`packages/auth/src/authClient.ts` still dual-writes the session JWT to
+localStorage ("Bearer fallback") alongside the HttpOnly cookie, and three
+pages read legacy token keys directly (`webapp/src/pages/Financials.tsx`
+`lst_token`; `CustomerHome.tsx` / `CustomerProfile.tsx` `ls_session`/`token`).
+Once all API callers send credentials via cookie only, delete the
+localStorage stash + the legacy reads. Not a dual-*writer* risk (it's the
+same session, one owner), but it widens the XSS blast radius — schedule with
+the next auth touch.
-- 
2.39.5

